Package: decoyfdr
Type: Package
Title: Matched Decoy Modules for False Discovery Rates of Gene-Expression Signatures
Version: 0.3.1
Authors@R: person("Gengtai", "Ye", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "337516242+drgengtaiye@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Estimates the false discovery rate of a claim about a library of gene-expression
    signatures, such as "k of these signatures predict the outcome", with the target-decoy design of
    peptide identification. Each signature (target) receives decoy modules of genes in no signature,
    matched to it on size, scoring engine, expression level and internal co-expression in every cohort;
    targets and decoys go through the identical test against size- and engine-matched random gene sets,
    and the decoys' call rate estimates how many target calls are false. The package also calibrates the
    estimate under the global null by permuting outcomes within cohorts. For prognostic risk models (Cox coefficients
    named by gene), check_models() tests each model and its matched decoys in validation cohorts under one rule and
    estimates how many validations are false; cohort_fvr() gives the false-validation rates of 41 public validation
    cohorts measured with null models.
